# Optional source configuration: copy this file to backend/.env.
# The API reads repository .env, then backend/.env; under an SDK webui/
# directory it also reads the SDK root .env first. Process variables win.
#
# The complete-app launcher passes this configuration to both child processes.
# For separate development servers, Vite reads backend/.env directly; restart
# the dev server after changing or removing an existing value.
# `pnpm start` alone does not read dotenv files: pass environment variables.
# Installed-package and Docker launches use environment variables and saved SDK
# settings rather than discovering .env files beside installed resources.
#
# Never prefix credentials with VITE_: those variables enter the browser bundle.
# HOST/PORT control the direct API/Node entry points. The complete-app launcher
# selects ports itself; use its --host, --port and --backend-port arguments.
#
# Server
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8000

# CORS — comma-separated origins allowed in dev. Neither supported way of running
# the app triggers CORS: `pnpm dev` routes the browser's /api through vite's proxy
# and `uv run webui` (like the Docker image) routes it through frontend/server.js,
# so in both cases the browser stays on one origin. This is the safety net for
# hand-rolled setups where a page served from somewhere else talks to this API
# directly — vite's dev port is the only such origin the repo itself can produce.
MS_AGENT_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Credentials for the `anthropic` provider (also used by any provider whose
# `protocol` is set to "anthropic", e.g. a DeepSeek /anthropic gateway).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- ms_agent backend LLM credentials (also used to bootstrap settings.json) ---
# Point at any OpenAI-compatible gateway (e.g. DashScope compatible-mode).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# Which provider/model the chat runtime uses when settings.json has no llm block.
# provider must be a known registry id: openai | modelscope | dashscope | zhipu |
# kimi | deepseek | minimax | openrouter | orcarouter | anthropic | google
# Keep the pair coherent — the model must exist AT that provider. A mismatch is
# not cosmetic: the model is registered under the provider and can shadow the
# correct one in the picker. qwen* models are DashScope/ModelScope, not OpenAI.
# First-run model bootstrap requires MS_AGENT_LLM_MODEL. Provider credentials
# are also available to the SDK independently of that bootstrap.
MS_AGENT_LLM_PROVIDER=dashscope
MS_AGENT_LLM_MODEL=qwen3.7-plus

# SDK home. Leave empty to share the SDK default (~/.ms_agent) with CLI/TUI,
# or set an isolated path such as ~/.ms_agent_webui.
MS_AGENT_HOME=

# Optional: third-party keys passed through to the SDK env (e.g. web-search MCP)
EXA_API_KEY=

# Where the LOCAL embedding model (fastembed ONNX, project memory in vector mode)
# is downloaded from on first use: modelscope (default, reachable without a
# HuggingFace proxy) or huggingface. An already-downloaded model is reused as-is.
MS_AGENT_EMBED_MODEL_SOURCE=modelscope

# --- Frontend (React Router SSR) ---
# Read in `../frontend/app/lib/env.ts` — the one module that touches process.env
# on the frontend side. HOST and PORT above are not read by vite, which takes its
# dev port from its own config; the production entry (`frontend/server.js`, used
# by `pnpm start` and `uv run webui`) does read them, for the port it serves on.

# Hosted deployment: 1 = this instance runs on a machine the user has no view of,
# so controls asking them to type an absolute path on it are hidden (the project
# location, and the "directory path" mode of the local skill import). Only the
# exact string 1 enables it; empty or unset keeps the local behaviour.
#
# Frontend-only: the backend does not read this and still accepts a path on the
# project and skill endpoints — it removes the entry points, not the ability.
MS_AGENT_FRONTEND_HOSTED_MODE=

# Where server-side frontend code reaches FastAPI. Two consumers that must agree:
# SSR loaders resolving relative /api paths (`../frontend/app/lib/api.ts`) and the
# dev-server proxy target for browser requests (`../frontend/vite.config.ts`). The
# value below IS the built-in default, so it can be left as is. Note this is a URL,
# unlike the HOST/PORT pair above that the backend binds to.
#
# `uv run webui` and the Docker image both override it, because they place the API
# on a port of their own choosing and SSR would otherwise fetch from whatever else
# happens to sit on 8000 — silently, since a failed loader degrades to empty data
# rather than an error page.
MS_AGENT_FRONTEND_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Not listed as a key above because nothing should set it by hand:
# MS_AGENT_WEBUI_BANNER=0 tells `frontend/server.js` to stay quiet about its own
# URL. `uv run webui` sets it for the child it spawns, so exactly one URL is
# printed — the one it prints itself, after the API answers.
